---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import HtmlEntityTool from '../../components/HtmlEntityTool.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="HTML Entity Encoder / Decoder" description="Convert special characters to HTML entities and back — prevent broken markup or XSS from unescaped input.">
  <HtmlEntityTool client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why this matters for security</h2>
  <p>Rendering unescaped user input as HTML can lead to XSS vulnerabilities. Encoding characters like &lt; and &gt; to their entity equivalents ensures they display as text rather than being interpreted as markup.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Encoding on input instead of output</strong>, causing double-encoding issues or storing already-encoded data that complicates later processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Relying only on entity encoding for security</strong> without also considering context-specific escaping (attributes, JavaScript, URLs each have different rules).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Safely rendering user-submitted text that may contain HTML-special characters</li>
    <li>Debugging why entity codes are showing up literally instead of rendering</li>
    <li>Decoding entities from a scraped or exported HTML source</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
